# Files two engine jobs both write that no driver above merges: a guide's or a breed's pictures, an album, a playlist, a
# page's summary card, the photo review page. A run that pulls main in keeps main's whole file, never one built from two
# versions. The push fallback (`git pull --rebase -X theirs`) merged them line by line and gave a part photo another
# photo's credit, and a still another still's caption and "no one in it" mark (8, 9, 15 and 16 Nov 2026). The run's
# change to such a file is dropped: a photo it put on the never-again list comes off again in the sweep after the pull,
# one it took off as another kind at the next photos run, and a still shows only with a verdict of its own (the verdicts
# merge per key). Only the engine's job scripts set this driver; elsewhere (leads' checkouts, GitHub's merges) these
# merge as text, as before. Not the pages' language files: main's whole file there would drop a hold the run added, and
# their holds follow main_holds (scripts/cycle-checks.sh).
content/guides/*/entity.json merge=main-whole
content/breeds/*/entity.json merge=main-whole
content/gallery/*.json merge=main-whole
content/series/*.json merge=main-whole
content/summaries/*.json merge=main-whole
docs/review/photo-subjects.md merge=main-whole
